<title>UK: Investcorp eyeing stg securitisation - paper.</title>
<headline>Investcorp eyeing stg securitisation - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bahrain-based Investcorp may securitise the cashflow from its recently acquired chain of British motorway service stations to finance the purchase, the Evening Standard newspaper said Thursday.</p>
<p>The paper said Investcorp could raise up to 350 million stg through a bond issue backed by the cashflows and assets of the Welcome Break chain.</p>
<p>The Evening Standard said Investcorp, which was being advised by Bankers Trust, was also looking at other forms of financing.</p>
<p>Investcorp paid Granada Plc 476 million stg for Welcome Break in February.</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
